# ============================================================
# PRIVATE — NEVER in the public repo (PII / maintainer-only).
# Public repo carries sanitized, generic content only. Anything that
# needs a real value at runtime reads it from .env (gitignored) or ships
# as a *.example twin. Standing PII-handling rules live in CLAUDE.local.md.
# (Treat every public repo as world-readable forever, git history included.)
# NOTE: gitignore has NO inline comments — keep patterns on their own lines.
# ============================================================
# All agent/working scaffolding (the reusable Open Engine how-to lives in integrations/open-engine/ instead)
.claude/
# Rich private ops doc + PII rules; the public CLAUDE.md is the slim sanitized one
CLAUDE.local.md
# Personal profile, colleague roster, work email
docs/curator.md
# Contains work email
routines/curator-daily.md
# Real launcher with local machine paths — public twin: start_brain.example.ps1
start_brain.ps1
# AJO-specific operational scripts — personal pipeline, not generic reusable code.
# The public repo carries a sanitized "build-it-yourself" how-to under integrations/
# instead (e.g. integrations/plaud-capture/), never the real script.
scripts/plaud-webhook.js
scripts/local-brain-worker.js
scripts/synthesize-persona.mjs
scripts/infer-entity-edges.mjs
scripts/plaud-curator-prompt.md
# Working drafts / design notes — unpolished, often about private pipeline pieces
docs/drafts/
# Head-of-Security baseline guide + the real do-not-publish terms list (private by
# definition — a list of what-never-to-share can't itself be shared). Parts 1-3 are
# generic and safe to copy into a public CLAUDE.md; Part 4 is the scrub list.
docs/CLAUDE-BASELINE-TEMPLATE.md
